# {{ project_name }}

{{ project_description }}

A self-contained MMIX assembly project. After generation, validation requires
only a GCC/Clang-compatible C compiler, `just`, and Git. macOS and Linux use
`cc`; On Windows run commands in Git Bash, with `clang` on PATH; Git supplies `sh`. Standard
POSIX shell utilities are used for orchestration. MSVC is not supported.
Copier and its Python runtime are only needed to generate the project.

```
just check
just init
just ci
just run
```

`just check` checks local prerequisites and committed source files. It never
installs or downloads anything. `just build` compiles the vendored MMIXware C
sources plus two small C99 guardrail executables. CWEB is not required.
MMIXware is compiled in its original C89 dialect; our guardrails compile with
`-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Werror`. See
[vendor provenance and license](vendor/mmixware/PROVENANCE.md).

## Validation

- `code-policy`: local lexical, entry-point, instruction, register, address,
  directive, and TRAP rules. See [the source policy](tools/POLICY.md).
- `code-artifacts`: checks tracked, untracked, and ignored paths. Generated
  objects, listings, and native binaries belong exclusively in ignored
  `build/`; no tracked build outputs are allowed.
- `code-object`: assembles `src/main.mms`, rejects any assembler diagnostics,
  runs `mmotype`, and requires contiguous code at `#100`, a Main symbol,
  the entry register, and data confined to the data segment.
- `test`: exact stdout text (native Windows CRLF translation) and empty stderr; simulator-script assertions of
  exit register `$255` and message memory; `.mml` instruction words matched
  against `mmotype`; `mmix -P` instruction coverage required at 100% using the
  object code as the denominator. Missing instructions cannot shrink coverage.
  Negative tests verify rejection of empty reports, warnings, and artifacts.
- `ci`: all of the above. No network, external rule packs, lint services,
  vulnerability feeds, GNU binutils, or containers are used.

The starter program prints `Hello, MMIX!` and exits zero. Update `tests/stdout.txt`
and the scripted state assertions in `scripts/test.sh` when changing its
contract. State commands live in `tests/state.txt`. These are real MMIX
simulator register/memory reads, not host-side approximations.

The initial module model is one standalone executable, `src/main.mms`; there
is no linking or include mechanism. The validator accepts a deliberately
restricted language subset rather than claiming to parse arbitrary MMIXAL.
Coverage measures executed instructions, not branches. This is a policy and
behavior suite, not a general security proof or secret scanner. `mmmix`,
mutation testing, and hardware timing analysis are not part of this template.

The GitHub Actions matrix executes on macOS, Linux, and Windows. Checkout and
installation of the declared `just` prerequisite use the network during runner
provisioning; all project validation after that is local. The runner provides
the C compiler and Git. No project dependencies are downloaded by `just`.

Build timestamps occur in MMO metadata and simulator register rN; binaries are
not claimed to be reproducible byte-for-byte. No checks depend on timestamps.
